     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:georgia,serif\">I&#39;m a PhD student attempting to analyze mark-recapture data using SECR. I have run into problems in importing my data, and was wondering if anyone could offer any assistance. I have a data set that spans 3 field seasons, with three trapping sessions per season, or 9 Occasions. Session was then broken down into trap night 1,2, or 3, or trap day which was entered as 4 or 5. Animal identifier is my ear tag ID, and location of the detection is my trap ID Eg. BG01-BG50. I have made sure that all ID cells have a value, and there are no blanks/dashes in the data set. Any blanks/dashes have received an NA. I have attached a snipping tool JPG with the first 37 entries as an example, and below is a short snippet of what my trap locations file looks like. I&#39;ve had no issues with trap locations.  </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:georgia,serif\">At this point I then try to import my data using the capthist function: </div><br><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:georgia,serif\">capturedata&lt;-make.capthist(EDF,trapfile,fmt=&quot;trapID&quot;,nocasions=NULL)</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:georgia,serif\">and I get the following error:</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:georgia,serif\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Reached total allocation of 6044Mb: see help(memory.size)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Reached total a